ong> Jan 19, 2026 at 6:03 AM\n   591→                </p>\n   592→                \n   593→            </header>\n   594→\n   595→            <div class=\"stats\">\n   596→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   597→                    <div class=\"value\">2,449</div>\n   598→                    <div class=\"label\">Words</div>\n   599→                </div>\n   600→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   601→                    <div class=\"value\">0h 16m</div>\n   602→                    <div class=\"label\">Est. Duration</div>\n   603→                </div>\n   604→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   605→                    <div class=\"value\">1</div>\n   606→                    <div class=\"label\">Chapters</div>\n   607→                </div>\n   608→                \n   609→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   610→                    <div class=\"value\">0</div>\n   611→                    <div class=\"label\">Main Characters</div>\n   612→                </div>\n   613→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   614→                    <div class=\"value\">73</div>\n   615→                    <div class=\"label\">Pronunciation Notes</div>\n   616→                </div>\n   617→            </div>\n   618→\n   619→            \n   620→            <section>\n   621→                <h2>📚 Book Structure</h2>\n   622→                \n   623→                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8;\">This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.</p>\n   624→                \n   625→                \n   626→            </section>\n   627→\n   628→            \n   629→            <section>\n   630→                <h2>📖 Plot Summary</h2>\n   631→                <div style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; white-space: pre-wrap;\">The story begins in the midst of a devastating plague known as the 'Red Death,' which spreads rapidly through the land, killing its victims with bleeding pores and scarlet stains, driving society into fear and isolation. Amid this chaos, Prince Prospero, a man of extravagant tastes and defiant spirit, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, abbey-like castle, sealing the gates to shield them from the outside horror. There, he constructs a world of opulence and distraction, hosting endless feasts, music, and revelry, attempting to deny the grim reality beyond his walls. The central setting—a series of seven uniquely colored rooms, each illuminated by stained-glass windows matching their hue—becomes a symbol of both beauty and entrapment, culminating in a final black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes each hour, momentarily halting all merriment.\n   632→\n   633→Months pass in this artificial paradise, until Prince Prospero hosts a grand masked ball, a spectacle of extravagance and illusion. The guests, cloaked in elaborate costumes, dance through the vibrant rooms, their joy undimmed by the ominous presence of the clock. Yet, as the midnight chime echoes through the halls, a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, with a corpse-like mask and robes dripping in blood. The figure moves silently through the rooms, inciting terror and outrage. The prince, consumed by rage and a sense of personal affront, pursues the intruder through each chamber, dagger in hand, determined to confront the blasphemy. His pursuit becomes a desperate, symbolic act of defiance against the inevitable.\n   634→\n   635→In the black chamber, the figure turns to face the prince, revealing nothing beneath the mask—only the truth of the plague’s presence. The prince collapses dead, a final collapse of arrogance and denial. The revelers, now realizing the horror they have ignored, rush into the chamber only to find the mask and robes empty, confirming the plague’s infiltration. One by one, they fall, succumbing to the very disease they had tried to escape. As the ebony clock stops its chime, darkness consumes the castle, and the final act of the story is complete: the illusion of safety shattered, and the inescapable nature of death revealed. The tale ends not with triumph, but with the chilling realization that no fortress, no wealth, no denial can shield one from fate.</div>\n   636→                \n   637→                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n   638→                    <strong>Themes:</strong> identity, ambition, loss\n   639→                </p>\n   640→                \n   641→            </section>\n   642→            \n   643→\n   644→            \n   645→            <section>\n   646→                <h2>🤖 Analysis Models</h2>\n   647→                <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; border-collapse: collapse;\">\n   648→                    <thead>\n   649→                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);\">\n   650→                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Phase</th>\n   651→                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Model</th>\n   652→                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Provider</th>\n   653→                        </tr>\n   654→                    </thead>\n   655→                    <tbody>\n   656→                        \n   657→                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--primary);\">\n   658→                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem;\">Chapter Detection</td>\n   659→                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem; font-family: monospace;\">qwen3:30b-instruct</td>\n   660→                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem;\">ollama</td>\n   661→                        </tr>\n   662→                        \n   663→                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--primary);\">\n   664→                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem;\">Char